      "fileName": "blast-lock.json",
      "id": "XLoRtMn48f2KKvsu",
      "name": "Blast Lock",
      "img": "icons/sundries/books/book-red-exclamation.webp",
      "type": "feat",
      "data": {
        "_id": "XLoRtMn48f2KKvsu",
        "folder": "KnXvyA7sSu2Rr2Hh",
        "img": "icons/sundries/books/book-red-exclamation.webp",
        "name": "Blast Lock",
        "system": {
          "actionType": {
            "value": "action"
          },
          "actions": {
            "value": 1
          },
          "category": "class",
          "description": {
            "value": "<p><strong>Requirements</strong> You're wielding a loaded firearm.</p>\n<hr />\n<p>Sometimes taking the shortest distance between two points involves removing an obstacle or two. You shoot your firearm at a lock within 10 feet. Make an attack roll against the DC required to @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.actionspf2e.Item.Pick a Lock]{Pick the Lock}</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Critical Success</strong> You open the lock, or you achieve two successes toward opening a complex lock.</p>\n<p><strong>Success</strong> You open the lock, or you achieve one success toward opening a complex lock.</p>\n<p><strong>Failure</strong> You fail to open the lock, and your shot makes it harder to open. Future attempts to Pick the Lock or Blast the Lock take a -2 circumstance penalty.</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> You fail to open the lock, and your shot makes it much harder to open. Future attempts to Pick the Lock or Blast the Lock take a -4 circumstance penalty.</p>"
          },
          "level": {
            "value": 1
          },
          "prerequisites": {
            "value": []
          },
          "publication": {
            "license": "ORC",
            "remaster": true,
            "title": "Pathfinder Guns & Gears"
          },
          "rules": [],
          "traits": {
            "rarity": "common",
            "value": [
              "attack",
              "gunslinger"
            ]
          }
        },
        "type": "feat"
      },
      "level": 1,
      "category": "class"
    },
    {
      "fileName": "cover-fire.json",
      "id": "IzkL60LlKzbKIhY1",
      "name": "Cover Fire",
      "img": "icons/sundries/books/book-red-exclamation.webp",
      "type": "feat",
      "data": {
        "_id": "IzkL60LlKzbKIhY1",
        "folder": "KnXvyA7sSu2Rr2Hh",
        "img": "icons/sundries/books/book-red-exclamation.webp",
        "name": "Cover Fire",
        "system": {
          "actionType": {
            "value": "action"
          },
          "actions": {
            "value": 1
          },
          "category": "class",
          "description": {
            "value": "<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per round</p>\n<p><strong>Requirements</strong> You're wielding a loaded firearm or crossbow.</p>\n<hr />\n<p>You lay down suppressive fire to protect allies by forcing foes to take cover from your wild attacks. Make a firearm or crossbow Strike; the target must decide before you roll your attack whether it will duck out of the way. If the target ducks, it gains a +2 circumstance bonus to AC against your attack, or a +4 circumstance bonus to AC if it has cover. It also takes a -2 circumstance penalty to ranged attack rolls until the end of its next turn. If the target chooses not to duck, you gain a +1 circumstance bonus to your attack roll for that Strike.</p>"
          },
          "frequency": {
            "max": 1,
            "per": "round",
            "value": 1
          },
          "level": {
            "value": 1
          },
          "prerequisites": {
            "value": []
          },
          "publication": {
            "license": "ORC",
            "remaster": true,
            "title": "Pathfinder Guns & Gears"
          },
          "rules": [],
          "traits": {
            "rarity": "common",
            "value": [
              "gunslinger"
            ]
          }
        },
        "type": "feat"
      },
      "level": 1,
      "category": "class"
    },
    {
      "fileName": "crossbow-crack-shot.json",
