    {
      "fileName": "sword-and-pistol.json",
      "id": "dWbISC0di0r4oPCi",
      "name": "Sword and Pistol",
      "img": "icons/sundries/books/book-red-exclamation.webp",
      "type": "feat",
      "data": {
        "_id": "dWbISC0di0r4oPCi",
        "folder": "KnXvyA7sSu2Rr2Hh",
        "img": "icons/sundries/books/book-red-exclamation.webp",
        "name": "Sword and Pistol",
        "system": {
          "actionType": {
            "value": "passive"
          },
          "actions": {
            "value": null
          },
          "category": "class",
          "description": {
            "value": "<p>You're comfortable wielding a firearm or crossbow in one hand and a melee weapon in the other, combining melee attacks with shots from the firearm. When you make a successful ranged Strike against an enemy within your reach with your one-handed firearm or one-handed crossbow, that enemy is @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.Off-Guard] against your next melee attack with a one-handed melee weapon.</p>\n<p>When you make a successful melee Strike against an enemy with your one-handed melee weapon, the next ranged Strike you make against that enemy with a one-handed firearm or one-handed crossbow doesn't trigger reactions that would trigger on a ranged attack but not a melee attack, such as Reactive Strike. Either of these benefits is lost if not used by the end of your next turn.</p>"
          },
          "level": {
            "value": 1
          },
          "prerequisites": {
            "value": []
          },
          "publication": {
            "license": "ORC",
            "remaster": true,
            "title": "Pathfinder Guns & Gears"
          },
